WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.310
Apple’s new iPad-specific OS, or iPadOS,
is coming this Fall and it’s bringing a

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.350
bunch of new features that make it more like
a computer than ever before, and this video

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:14.530
is a full guide on how to use the new split-view
and multi-tasking features, so let’s get

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.530
started.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.330
Multitasking starts with the app dock, so
let’s fill it up with the apps we use every

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.330
day.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:23.311
Something new this year is the ability to
put entire app folders onto the dock, so you

00:00:23.311 --> 00:00:26.449
can have access to any app you want from just
the dock.

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:31.090
Starting with Slide Over mode, first open
an app, then swipe up from the bottom to bring

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.160
up the dock.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.069
Then Drag an app onto the side of the screen,
but don’t drag it to the very edge.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:40.899
You can now use both apps at the same time,
or drag items from one app into the other.

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:43.079
Like images, links, or files.

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:47.399
You can also swipe the bar on the bottom of
the Slide Over window to switch between other

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:51.699
apps you have open in Slide Over mode, Or
you can swipe up on that bar to show all of

00:00:51.699 --> 00:00:54.749
the apps at once and choose which one you’d
like to use.

00:00:54.749 --> 00:00:58.829
You can also drag the top of the Slide Over
window to the other side of the screen.

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:03.340
Slide over mode is very useful for doing things
like quickly bringing up the Files app and

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.780
dragging files into apps like Lumafusion for
video editing.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.760
If you don’t have the desired app open in
one of your Slide Over windows, just drag

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.280
the app from the dock and it’ll replace
the current app.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.880
Once you’re finished, just grab the edge
of the window and slide it off the screen,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.630
and swipe again to bring it back.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:23.799
To switch to Split-View mode, just pull the
top bar down and into the edge of the screen.

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:27.719
At that point, you can bring back the Slide
Over window by swiping from the edge, and

00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:30.320
you can move it to the other side, just as
before.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.390
And pulling down on the Slide Over apps top
bar will replace the underlying split-view

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:35.390
app.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.939
Now in split-view mode, you can easily swap
the positions of the apps by dragging the

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:39.860
top bar of an app to the other side.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:44.210
You can also drag the bar in center of the
apps to give more space to either app, either

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.469
in a 50/50 or 25/75 split.

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:51.350
To replace an app while in split-view, just
drag it from the app dock.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:55.729
You can even use the same app on both sides
of the screen, which is useful for transferring

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:59.799
files in the Files app, and it should work
for third-party apps as well like Microsoft

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:03.869
Word, but it doesn’t seem to be working
yet in this first beta of iPadOS.

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:07.420
Within the notes app, you can even grab a
note and drag it to the side of the screen

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.580
to open both Notes side-by-side.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:14.640
While the mail app is open, you can compose
a new email and drag the compose view to side

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.100
in either slide over or split-view mode.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.920
Hit cancel or send and it’ll automatically
close.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.300
The coolest part is that you can swipe along
the bottom of the screen to swipe between

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.310
apps, and all of the different split-view
app combinations you previously had open will

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.150
be saved, including as many versions of each
app as you’d like.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.390
You can also swipe with 4 fingers instead
to switch between apps, or swipe up to get

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:39.730
to the home screen, or swipe up and stop at
the center to open the app switcher and choose

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.020
the app you want to use.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.391
If you want to exit split-view mode, just
pull down on one of the apps tabs to get it

00:02:45.391 --> 00:02:47.650
into slide over mode, then swipe it off the
screen.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:51.550
Now let’s say you’re at the home screen
and want to start a fresh version of an app,

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.720
but it keeps opening up the same app that’s
already in split-view.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.280
Well, simply tap and hold on an app in the
the dock or on the home screen, and tap Show

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.540
all windows to open the App exposé.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.660
From here, you’ll see the various versions
of the app currently open, and you can swipe

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.470
to close them, or tap the plus icon to start
fresh.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:11.880
If you want to get back to a different version
of the app you’re currently using, just

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.750
tap the same app within the app dock and it’ll
open up that same app exposé.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:21.850
Now in Safari, we finally get automatic desktop
mode for browsing, and to split-view, just

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:25.130
tap and hold on a tab and drag it to the edge
of the screen.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:29.970
You can also watch videos in picture in picture
mode if the video player supports it by tapping

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.050
the PIP button.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:34.520
You can now swipe between apps and use your
iPad while the video plays.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.030
You can tap to pause, close, or bring it back
to the safari window.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:42.520
You can also drag it to any corner of the
screen, and spread with two fingers to make

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.630
the vidoe larger.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:47.820
You can use PIP on YouTube, but it will only
play while that tab is open and you can’t

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.860
move it around, but it’s useful if you want
to browse YouTube.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.310
Apple’s also added some text editing features
that can really speed up your workflow.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.120
You can quickly pick up your cursor with one
finger and move it around anywhere you’d

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.820
like, or use two fingers anywhere on the screen.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.860
You can also tap multiple times to select
different amounts of text.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.620
Tap twice to select a word.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:12.860
Tap 3 times, or for some reason 4 times in
this beta version, to select a sentence and

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.620
tap 4 times, or for us, 5 times to select
an entire paragraph.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:22.280
You can then pinch with three fingers to copy,
and then spread with three fingers to paste.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:26.920
To undo, you don’t have to shake it anymore,
just swipe left with three fingers, and then

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.090
swipe right with three fingers to redo.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:33.130
And finally, you can pinch with two fingers
on the keyboard to shrink it, and then grab

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:36.820
the tab to move it wherever you’d like on
the screen, allowing you to type with just

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:40.450
one thumb, or use the new swipe keyboard feature..

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:44.220
Then you can pinch with two fingers again
to bring it back to the full keyboard.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.350
So that was everything you need to know about
Multitasking in Apple’s new iPadOS.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:52.280
If this video helped you out, tap like and
click the circle above to subscribe.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:05:00.720
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video!

